# Run outputs are not tracked. Only the curated baseline is.
#
# `pnpm mcp:audit` (scripts/mcp-audit.ts) and `pnpm tsx scripts/okx-seller-smoke.ts`
# write three files per run into this directory, and they accumulate: by
# 2026-10-04 there were 108 untracked ones from three days of runs, showing up
# in every `git status` and in none of the checks.
#
# `README.md` already says the artifacts are reproducible — "re-run the script
# to regenerate them" — so the directory's tracked content is the *record*, and
# a fresh run is not a change to the record. The 2026-07-20 baseline stays
# tracked: `.gitignore` never untracks a file that is already in the index.
#
# To cite a new run in the README, promote it deliberately:
#
#     git add -f screenshots/mcp-audit-octocat-Hello-World-full-<timestamp>.json
#
mcp-audit-*.html
mcp-audit-*.json
mcp-audit-*.md
mcp-audit-*.png
okx-seller-smoke-*.html
okx-seller-smoke-*.json
okx-seller-smoke-*.md
okx-seller-smoke-*.png
